{"name":"Quicksand","hex":"#ac9884","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quicksand","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Wet sand that appears firm but in which things readily sink, often found near rivers or coasts.","Anything that metaphorically pulls one down or buries one; a treacherous, risky danger"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quicksand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quicksand","blocks":[{"text":"Quicksand, also known as sinking sand, is a colloid consisting of fine granular material and water. It forms in saturated loose sand when the sand is suddenly agitated. When water in the sand cannot escape, it creates a liquefied soil that loses strength and cannot support weight. Quicksand can form in standing water or in upward flowing water. In the case of upward-flowing water, forces oppose the force of gravity and suspend the soil particle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Quicksand_warning.jpg/330px-Quicksand_warning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quicksand","wikidata":"Q224090"},{"title":"Quicksand (American band)","blocks":[{"text":"Quicksand is an American post-hardcore band from New York City, founded in 1990. Their debut self-titled EP was followed by two major-label albums, Slip (1993) and Manic Compression (1995). Quicksand's sound has been compared to that of Fugazi and Helmet. The band supported their releases with extensive touring but fell short of the mainstream success anticipated by their labels. These factors and internal stress led them to separate first in 1995 and again in 1999 following a failed year-and-a-half reunion. Quicksand reunited once again in 2012, and has since released three more albums: Interiors (2017), Distant Populations (2021) and Bring On the Psychics (2026)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Quicksand_Rock_am_Ring_2014_%2848%29.JPG/330px-Quicksand_Rock_am_Ring_2014_%2848%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quicksand_(American_band)","wikidata":"Q728559"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Quicksand_%284596511338%29.jpg/500px-Quicksand_%284596511338%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Quicksand_%284596511338%29.jpg/500px-Quicksand_%284596511338%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Quicksand on the Thames","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuicksand_(4596511338).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Stuck_in_Quicksand_%2813944309974%29.jpg/500px-Stuck_in_Quicksand_%2813944309974%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Stuck_in_Quicksand_%2813944309974%29.jpg/1280px-Stuck_in_Quicksand_%2813944309974%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Stuck_in_Quicksand_%2813944309974%29.jpg/500px-Stuck_in_Quicksand_%2813944309974%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A group of hikers encountering quicksand on the banks of the Paria River, Utah","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStuck_in_Quicksand_(13944309974).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Quicksandwarning.JPG/500px-Quicksandwarning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Quicksandwarning.JPG/1280px-Quicksandwarning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum